\n52\t\n53\t**Reviewer's note:** No retrieval corpus or search index exists in the code and the manifest states retrieval none\n54\t\n55\t(no evidence cited)\n56\t\n57\t## R04.4\n58\t\n59\t**Check:** Code can quarantine, expire, and revoke chunks, and it also clears or invalidates search caches.\n60\t\n61\t**How to verify:** 1) Find quarantine, expiry, and revoke code (`delete`, `quarantine`, `ttl`, `expires_at`). 2) Check search excludes those chunks and caches are cleared. 3) Answer no if any of the three operations is missing, or caches (query cache, embedding cache) are not invalidated.\n62\t\n63\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n64\t\n65\t**Reviewer's note:** No retrieval corpus or search index exists in the code and the manifest states retrieval none\n66\t\n67\t(no evidence cited)\n68\t\n69\t## Your answer\n70\t\n71\tWrite this JSON to R04.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"R04\"):\n72\t```json\n73\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n74\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R04.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n75\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n76\t```\n77\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed79c226-9ca0-4985-836b-16cb4530c091","uuid":"2c81d4f3-1a57-4430-aacc-91157974aeb1","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:47:34.307Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-813rqtfh/sheet.md","content":"# N/A challenge: R04